/E (One of the primary challenges lies in balancing respect for cultural traditions with the universality of human rights. Some States argue that international human rights norms should be interpreted in light of national cultural and religious values. Others contend that allowing cultural exceptions risks undermining universally recognised rights, particularly those relating to women and girls. The Commission must consider how to encourage cultural sensitivity while ensuring that fundamental rights remain protected. )
